<p>
<font size=5>Monitoring Activities</font><br>
<b>Pocket Water Inc. (PWI) and UI Eco-Hydraulics Group</b>
<p>
During the month of July the monitoring effort was coordinated closely with UI students.  Three field visits were made to Red River in July, two by Dave Fuhrman and one by Steve Bauer.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>GROUNDWATER MONITORING</b></font>. There are now a total of 14 ground water wells installed on the meadow.  The total depth of each of the wells was measured, and the depth-to-water level for each well has been measured and recorded a total of three times.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>TURBIDITY AND STAGE MONITORING</b></font>.  Turbidity and river stage data from station RDN (located near the abandoned bridge in the WMA) was downloaded periodically throughout the month.  Data from the month of June has been processed, and the July data processing is in progress.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>DISCHARGE MONITORING</b></font>. We routinely make a manual measurement of flow to develop the stage-discharge rating curve for a station, relating discharge to the river stage.  UI performed two discharge estimates at station RDN.  This data was used with additional data from PWI to produce a preliminary rating curve This rating curve will be continually updated as additional data is collected.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>TEMPERATURE CALIBRATION</b></font>. Temperature is measured at the six temperature gauges using a certified digital thermometer. These measurements were taken at two different times and recorded.  This data will be compared with data from the data loggers to ensure they are reading properly.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>PHOTOPOINTS</b></font>.  During the week of July 6th, Steve took pictures at the photopoint locations.  These slides have been filed for comparison to previous periods.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>REVEGETATION/EROSION CONTROL SUCCESS</b></font>.  Steve and Kurt established transects and surveyed sites disturbed during 1997 construction to evaluate erosion control success.  In general, grass seed coverage was good on all constructed areas except the area inside Giant Bend curve.  In this zone there are pockets of scour that eroded surface soils and removed the seed that was planted.  
<p>
Kurt collected the data on plant survival within the revegetation success transects and sent this information to Steve for incorporation into the monitoring report.
<p>
<font face="arial" size=2><b>1997 MONITORING REPORT</b></font>.  PWI and UI have been working on completion of the 1997 draft report.  Gloria Beattie at UI has been able to use the GIS data to develop some report figures for displaying monitoring locations in the draft report.  She has also been working on interpretation of information on stream channel conditions.  The effort in completing the monitoring report is progressing. 


